// Run with GC logging to SEE Minor vs Major/Full GC events:
//   java -Xlog:gc -Xmx64m MinorVsMajorDemo
public class MinorVsMajorDemo {
    static byte[] longLived; // promoted to Old Gen -> touched by Major GC

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        longLived = new byte[10 * 1024 * 1024]; // survives -> promoted

        for (int i = 0; i < 2000; i++) {
            byte[] shortLived = new byte[1024 * 1024]; // dies fast -> Minor GC
            // shortLived is unreachable next iteration; Young Gen reclaims it
        }
        System.out.println("Done; log shows 'Pause Young' vs 'Pause Full'");
    }
}
```
`Pause Young` lines are Minor GC (frequent, short); `Pause Full` lines are Major/Full GC (rare, long).

